| actual lo | actual hi | actual mid | compared abscissa | go right |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0 | 2 | 1 | 2 | false |
| 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | true |

Actual distances: 1 and 1. Selected sample: 0, value: 10.
\image(figures/nearest_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual binary-search decisions and lower-index midpoint tie.)
\alttext(The final distances are both one, so sample0 and ordinate10 are selected.)

> Retain the original smooth-function samples

The original function is sin(x)+0.3x, sampled at0,0.8,...,6.4. The original
queries1.4 and1.0 choose the nodes1.6 and0.8 respectively. The native study
generates the same coarse samples and a321-point grid with spacing0.02 over the
same domain. Integer-generated query coordinates avoid accumulated loop-step
drift.

A line through dense nearest-neighbor values approximates the staircase
visually; each steep connector is a drawing between neighboring grid
evaluations, not an interpolated transition supplied by the model. The table
verifies exact node reproduction. The smooth reference is retained to show the
lost intermediate values rather than to claim the staircase reconstructs the
unknown function exactly.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nearest_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nearest_neighbor_interpolation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::algorithms::nearest_neighbor_demo_study();
    dm::algorithms::NearestNeighborInterpolant model(s.samples.xs, s.samples.ys);
    std::print("| original node | actual stored value | native query at node |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.samples.xs.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", s.samples.xs[i], s.samples.ys[i],
                   model.evaluate(s.samples.xs[i]));
    std::print("\nOriginal query1.4: {}. Query1.0: {}.\n", model.evaluate(1.4),
               model.evaluate(1.0));
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(s.queries, s.truth, "smooth reference", {107, 114, 128}, 2).line(
        s.queries, s.values, "nearest samples", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(
        s.samples.xs, s.samples.ys, "original nodes", {220, 38, 38}, 6).y_limits(-.2, 2.7).title("Original nine-node nearest-neighbor staircase").x_label("query x").y_label("value").save_svg("build/nearest_original.svg");
}
```
