> Endpoint, singleton and empty controls

The prepared API requires equal-size finite arrays and strictly increasing
abscissae. Singleton input always returns its one ordinate for a finite query.
Matching empty arrays preserve the legacy zero return, explicitly a placeholder
rather than an estimated observation. Nonfinite queries throw even for an empty
model. Widened distance arithmetic prevents unnecessary intermediate overflow
for large finite coordinates.

The trace owns both node arrays and its actual search records. Capture
counts2n+2 base units for nodes/query/result plus one per actual search step,
default1000000; zero disables. Admission precedes history copies/appends, and
failure returns no partial trace. Its storage includes copied nodes, even when
an endpoint requires no search loop. The model itself validates in O(n), owns
O(n) data and answers finite queries in O(log(n+1)) work with constant
query-driver storage.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nearest_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nearest_neighbor_interpolation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::NearestNeighborInterpolant model({0, 2}, {10, 20});
    std::vector<double> x{-2, 0, 1, 1.5, 2, 4}, y;
    std::print("| finite query | actual selected index | actual value | actual route | endpoint tests | " "search steps |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (double q : x) {
        auto t = model.trace(q);
        y.push_back(t.value);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", q, t.selected, t.value,
                   t.route, t.endpoint_tests, t.steps.size());
    }
    dm::algorithms::NearestNeighborInterpolant empty({}, {}), single({3}, {7});
    std::print("\nEmpty placeholder: {}. Singleton at query−100: {}.\n",
               empty.evaluate(0), single.evaluate(-100));
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual selected values", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "Nearest-sample controls: tie and endpoint selection").x_label(
        "finite query").y_label("stored ordinate returned").save_svg(
        "build/nearest_controls.svg");
}
```
