\alttext(Finite out-of-range queries use endpoint ordinates; the exact midpoint belongs to the lower sample.)

> Conclusion and references

Actual search records explain nearest selection without report-side binary
search. The original staircase demonstrates preserved values and lost
smoothness; the error study connects its spacing to a Lipschitz argument.
Complete validation, prepared-model costs and explicit empty/tie/endpoint
conventions define the native API's practical behavior.

[SciPy interp1d documentation|https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.interpolate.interp1d.html]
provides a software comparison for lower-neighbor rounding at nearest-neighbor
half-way ties. This implementation uses its own prepared binary-search producer,
validation and endpoint contract.

